"7. A piping hydrotest requires the system to be filled with water at ambient temperature. The design temperature of the system is 350°C with a design pressure of 50 bar. What is the minimum hydrostatic test pressure per ASME B31.3 for this system?",
"75 bar — ASME B31.3 para 345.4.2 requires 1.5× design pressure for all hydrotest conditions.\n83 bar — ASME B31.3 para 345.4.2 requires 1.5× design pressure multiplied by the allowable stress ratio (σ at ambient / σ at design temperature) when the ratio exceeds 1.0.\n62.5 bar — ASME B31.3 para 345.4.2 requires 1.25× design pressure for systems at elevated temperatures.\n50 bar — the design pressure is used directly for elevated temperature hydrotest conditions.",
"83 bar — ASME B31.3 para 345.4.2 requires 1.5× design pressure multiplied by the allowable stress ratio (σ at ambient / σ at design temperature) when the ratio exceeds 1.0.",
